ages in development and application of tungsten carbides, ceramics, and hard materials and solutions worldwide. It operates through two segments, Metal Cutting and Infrastructure. The Metal Cutting segment provides milling, hole making, turning, threading, and toolmaking systems used in the manufacture of airframes, aero engines, trucks and automobiles, ships, and various types of industrial equipment under the Kennametal, WIDIA, WIDIA Hanita, and WIDIA GTD brands through its direct sales force, a network of independent and national distributors, integrated supplier channels, and digitally. Its Infrastructure segment produces engineered tungsten carbide and ceramic components, earth-cutting tools, and metallurgical powders, such as compacts, nozzles, frac seats, and custom components used in oil and gas and petrochemical industries; rod blanks and abrasive water jet nozzles for general industries; earth cutting tools and systems used in underground mining, trenching and foundation drilling, and road milling; tungsten carbide powders for the oil and gas, aerospace, and process industries; high temperature critical wear components, tungsten penetrators, and armor solutions for aerospace and defense; and ceramics used by the packaging industry for metallization of films and papers under the Kennametal brand through a direct sales force and distributors. The company was founded in 1938 and is based in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Sanjay K. Chowbey | President, CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $291K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Kennametal Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.6B market cap on $2.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 32%.","The company is burning through $81M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +10.9% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 17\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 4.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +10.9% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Price sits 18% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.17611293657019148},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 8% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 11% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 78% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Insiders are net buyers (67% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How (KMT) Movements Inform Risk Allocation Models","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/12/How_KMT_Movements_Inform_Risk_Allocation_Models_111926053401_1795084441.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795084441.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Kennametal (NYSE:KMT) Faces Pressure As Market Sentiment Weakens","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/industrial/kennametal-nysekmt-faces-pressure-as-market-sentiment-weakens","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795073760.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.791,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Kennametal (KMT) Could Be 11% Undervalued After Strong Quarterly Results","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-kmt/ke