undamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Capex runs only 0.5x depreciation (3.3% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 0, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.8%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insider trading is two-way: 4 purchases and 2 sales over the past year, net $337K sold.","It returns 4.3% a year to shareholders (0.6% in buybacks and 3.8% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.6% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 39 consecutive years, though it has been cut 1.8% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 8,100 employees, each generates about $291K of revenue, 0.8x the Industrials median.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$10K per employee.","CEO pay is $2.6M (9x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $4K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":55,"head":"Avoid: earns below its cost of capital and burns cash.","pros":["Composite 50, above the 39 line (gates 15/26)","Net debt/EBITDA 1.0x","P/E 2.8x vs sector 22.1x","EV/EBITDA 2.8x vs sector 12.9x","7 analysts' mean target $27.57 (+30%)"],"cons":["Trades 18% above fair value of $18.10","ROIC 8.0% vs WACC 8.6%","FCF margin 3.4% (burns cash)"],"flags":["Earns below its cost of capital and burns cash"],"need":[],"buy_below":15.39,"vc":{"base":18.1,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":18.1,"n_alt":3,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.2959,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":22.1377,"ev_ebitda":12.904,"pfcf":21.8001,"pb":2.7623,"roic":0.0997,"gross_margin":0.2864,"fcf_margin":0.0677,"div_yield":0.0151}},"ticker":"KMT","date":"2026-11-20"}